@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title Plant equipment authoring with explicit source generation (specification 39, §10, §21.3, §21.9)
actor Engineer
component "HMI canvas and inspector\nTag, hardware status, key settings" as Editor
component "HIR declaration index\nTypes, members, initialisers and defaults" as Declarations
component "Component definitions (hmi/pairs)\nSymbol, panel, settings, terminals, dependencies" as Components
artifact "Library hmi/\npanels, pairs, symbols" as Library
component "My equipment (language server)\nOwn blocks: plain device + automatic panel,\nor the Plant base's definition" as Own
component "Create PLC code\nOne declaration + one call per device;\na PID loop as ordinary code around Control.PID" as Generate
component "Create HMI\nDeclared devices not on a page" as Propose
component "Runtime page writer\nOne page format" as Writer
component "Version-checked WorkspaceEdit" as Edit
artifact "HMI pages / panels / screen.toml" as Pages
artifact "plant.toml\nBlock, settings, signals, dependencies" as Design
artifact "PLC source\nCustomer code + checksum-marked regions\n(declarations, retained declarations, calls)" as Source
component "Explicit Build and Deploy\nFiles sent as written" as Build
Engineer --> Editor
Editor --> Declarations : inspect without compilation or PLC execution
Editor --> Components
Library --> Components : a project file of the same name wins
Declarations --> Own : own blocks, members, BOOL methods
Own --> Editor : listed under My equipment
Editor --> Edit : first placement: pair + panel; picture: definition + placed objects
Editor --> Pages : drawing edits
Editor --> Edit : inspector change: plant.toml + regions of a generated device
Source --> Declarations : parsed declarations, including unsaved source
Engineer --> Generate : explicit button
Pages --> Generate : shown devices (block + instance)
Design --> Generate
Components --> Generate : terminals, dependencies, call order
Declarations --> Generate : declared and hand-written instances
Generate --> Edit : declarations and calls; USING for loop code; loop write rules for runtime.toml
Engineer --> Propose : explicit button
Declarations --> Propose
Components --> Propose : definition by type or nearest base
Propose --> Writer
Writer --> Edit : new views only
Edit --> Pages
Edit --> Design
Edit --> Source
Source --> Build : separate deliberate action
note bottom of Editor
Settings show the declaration's initial value, else the block's default;
a new device shows the plant.toml choice. No probes or preview scans.
end note
note bottom of Generate
A region changed by hand is refused with its line; a renamed one is
accepted. Hand-declared instances are reused, never redeclared.
No helper variables, identities or registration, except a loop's own
variables beside its PID (TIC101_Setpoint, TIC101_Parameters). Idempotent.
end note
@enduml
